# pyro_configure

- Label: Pyro Configure
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 9 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_configure.html
- Summary (EN): Sets up the starting configuration of a Pyro simulation by determining its voxel size. Also generates placeholder VDBs that give Pyro Block Begin the reference field it needs. Output is vdb_ref, the VDB reference controlling the initial voxel size.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Configure fixe la taille des voxels d'une simulation Pyro et fournit la référence de volume attendue par Pyro Block Begin.

- Inputs meaning: ["vdb_ref (optional): float VDB used to set the voxel size", "camera_ref: camera reference, used only when Divisions is set to Coverage", "centroid_ref: point geometry marking the center of the simulation, used only when Divisions is set to Coverage"]

- Key parameters: ["Divisions: Voxel Size uses world units and suits fully 3D simulations; Resolution derives voxel size from a default 2-unit square imaging plane (voxel size = 2 / Resolution); Coverage sizes voxels from camera resolution and distance so invisible detail is not simulated", "Voxel Size: size of one voxel in world coordinates", "Resolution: simulation resolution when it fills the standard imaging plane", "Pixel Coverage: number of screen pixels covering one voxel; default 2.5", "Min Voxel Size: when enabled, prevents voxels from becoming smaller than a set minimum (labeled Min Vozel Size on the page)"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "camera_ref and centroid_ref matter only in Coverage mode"]

